From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: a framed Linux program's own minimize button, its coming forward, and its active look

Three things a window manager does for a Linux program's window that its
Wine frame (0762) did not:

- Its own minimize button (GTK's header bar, SG Office's, Firefox's beside
  its tabs) asks the window manager to minimize it (WM_CHANGE_STATE,
  XIconifyWindow): nobody answered for a framed window, and the button did
  nothing. Its frame is now minimized, as by its own button, and the
  program is told it is (WM_STATE Iconic, _NET_WM_STATE_HIDDEN), and
  Normal again when restored (a maximized one is not told it is restored
  while minimized).
- A program bringing its window forward itself (_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW: GTK's
  gtk_window_present, Firefox handed a link by another program, a second
  start of a program showing its first window) was ignored: its frame is
  now restored if minimized and made the active window.
- The session's window manager (wlroots' xwm) says _NET_WM_STATE_FOCUSED is
  kept, so GTK draws a window active or inactive (greyed header bar) by it
  alone; for a framed window it was never kept: always inactive once we
  had written its state (maximized, restored), or always active as the
  window manager left it. It is now kept as a window manager keeps it:
  the program's window has the X focus, or not (a move of the focus
  inside it, or a keyboard grab's -- Alt+Tab -- changes nothing).

Test: test/linuxembed-gate.sh 4b, 5d, 5e (with test/netwm-fullscreen.c's
new iconify and activate requests and the probe's iconic and minimize).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_EMBED_NO_FOCUSED_STATE fails 4b, SG_MUTANT_EMBED_NO_ICONIFY
5d, SG_MUTANT_EMBED_NO_ACTIVE_WINDOW 5e (dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c).
